        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/6de8d8/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2020-09-03T22:00:43.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This niche case has come up in a forum game on BGG and I&nbsp;wondered if anyone had a definitive ruling.</p>\n<p><em>Devious Disruption</em> states, \"Baron Blade deals each Hero target X Lightning damage, where X = 3 plus the number of Hero Ongoing and Equipment cards still in play\".</p>\n<p>Tachyon keeps&nbsp;<em>Synaptic Interruption&nbsp;</em>in play and redirects the first damage back to Baron Blade, destroying Synaptic Interruption in the process. Does the subsequent&nbsp;damage Baron Blade inflicts get reduced by 1, as there is now one less Ongoing card in play, or does it stay the same, based on the cards in play when X was first calculated?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:54:15.410Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
